r of Permutations of Objects Chosen From a Group Fewer Than Ten"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aaed84db-333e-5211-84c5-2d24c1d90316" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,016" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394622} {:answer/id #uuid "e1c1b16c-2ec4-5950-92f8-59f867978e1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,024" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394623} {:answer/id #uuid "542940cc-ac17-5702-9c22-d185b7bb47c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394624} {:answer/id #uuid "2e70f827-6004-57e0-825e-f0e45fc164d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,344" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394625} {:answer/id #uuid "3d0a0e84-7492-5601-b7a4-02b8e70ea90d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\,120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1c1b16c-2ec4-5950-92f8-59f867978e1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,024" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394623} :answer-field/id #uuid "72d9fa78-c6ea-5ff0-a6cb-0b7ec2cbcfc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ef67e9d-56e9-502f-9f38-dd41f4d01e7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-84983" :question/problem "A bag contains $9$ different colored marbles. Jamie takes $4$ marbles from the bag, one at a time, and puts them in the order they were taken from the bag to create a sequence of colors. How many different sequences of colors are possible?" :question/worked-solution "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $9$ colored marbles, so $n=9.$ We want to select $4$ of those marbles to make a sequence of colors, so we have $r=4.$ \n\nTherefore, the number of different ways to choose the marbles is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{9}{P}_{4} & =\\frac{9!}{(9-4)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{9!}{5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot \\cancel{5!}}{\\cancel{5!}} \\\\  & =9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =3\\,024.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
